./docs/v5_validation_report.md:18:Market reapplies the inherited sale-block ordering optimizer after all later layers have finalized the market action. It only rearranges contiguous SELL orders; quantities, worker commands, purchases and hiring barriers remain fixed. It tests order permutations under the inherited model of an opponent with the same planned sales and stock, maximizing the modeled revenue difference. That opponent model is an approximation, not recovered hidden information. The final pass prevents later sale additions from undoing an earlier order optimization. The idea was informed by [Tetsutani’s public notebook](https://www.kaggle.com/code/tetsutani/demand-preserving-turn-sale-timing).
./docs/v5_validation_report.md:20:Guarded applies that extra pass only when the opponent’s visible productive farm layout has at least 85% similarity. Empty plots do not create artificial similarity, and at least eight productive positions are required. This is a conservative gate on a clone-based market model; it is not a learned opponent identity.
./docs/v5_validation_report.md:26:6,784 reacting local games across 232 distinct new world seeds: three selection generations and 3,040 frozen confirmation games across 168 worlds. Both seats were used. All planned games completed, with zero callback failures and unchanged candidate/opponent/harness hashes. The official interpreter was 1.32.7 with natural shop generation.
./docs/v5_validation_report.md:34:## Fresh confirmation: ordinary public opponents
./docs/v5_validation_report.md:36:64 fresh worlds, six reacting opponents, both seats: 768 games per controller.
./docs/v5_validation_report.md:87:## Independent-code opponents: weaker stress group
./docs/v5_validation_report.md:101:Intervals resample complete world blocks containing both seats and all opponents. They condition on this fixed suite; they do not sample unknown future strategies. The public opponents share substantial controller ancestry. The two Lonespear variants form one independent, weaker family. Opening attackers are related stress variants. Their results are reported separately rather than used to inflate the ordinary-opponent score.
./docs/v5_validation_report.md:107:No finalist exceeded the predeclared ordinary-opponent subgroup regression or severe-loss veto in confirmation.
./docs/v5_validation_report.md:115:Ten of 35 sampled listed losses showed a cash shortage, missed hires, and an escaping cow; none of 24 selected winning controls did. Reproducing all 7,190 original actions across those ten losses and changing only the opening restored the hires and retained the animal every time. Fixed-opponent counterfactual scores were not used for promotion. The integer opening grid tested 14,641 buy/sell combinations per choice: the eight/three opening stayed above the required staffing budget; v4 fell below it in 897 cases.
