./docs/stability_report.md:40:### Every public opponent
./docs/stability_report.md:68:Lonespear and Big Herd share an implementation family with each other but are independently implemented from the tape-based main agents. They are weaker stress opponents; easy wins here do not establish top-tier strength.
./docs/stability_report.md:83:Complete first-shop strata, worst individual games, score intervals and perfect-world Wilson bounds are in the machine-readable reports. Shop strata are post-hoc diagnostics. Bootstrap intervals condition on this frozen suite; they do not represent uncertainty over future opponent strategies. All-win bootstrap intervals are degenerate, not proof of certainty.
./docs/stability_report.md:98:None of the four sampled winning replays had early animal losses or failed placements. This is useful diagnostic contrast but remains a tiny, selected sample with different opponents. The large real-game loss regimes are poorly represented by the easier local public panel; more clone games cannot resolve that coverage gap.
./docs/stability_report.md:110:The advice to use more games and fresh seeds was retained in AGENTS.md, with qualifications: use the same seeds across candidates inside a comparison; rotate seeds between confirmation rounds; count independent worlds and opponent families; evaluate tails and subgroup regressions; and consume a holdout once it informs selection. More clone games alone cannot resolve strategic overfitting.
./docs/stability_report.md:112:The interrupted first attempt is excluded entirely. The original fixed plans were rerun under new filenames because the operating system refused reads of the partial log. No candidates, opponents, seeds or budgets were selected from partial scores. These completed results are now consumed evidence, not an untouched test set for future tuning.
